---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTA from '../../../components/CTA.astro';
import MermaidFlow from '../../../components/MermaidFlow.astro';

const lang = 'en';

const agentWorkflow = `
%%label: Agent Workflow
%%note: Discover · Build · Execute
graph LR
  Discover["Agent<br/>Discover<br/>Queries valid indexed paths matching user intent. Surfaces missing fields. Handles ambiguity before building the query."]
  Build["Agent<br/>Build<br/>Constructs a typed query object: filters, sorting, aggregations. Structurally valid by construction. No SQL generated."]
  Execute["System<br/>Execute<br/>Compiles the query to validated SQL and runs it. Returns a stable cursor for pagination, even if the data changes mid-session."]
  Discover --> Build --> Execute
`;
---
<Layout
  title="SURF: Hybrid Search for Orchestrator-Core"
  description="How Virge collaborated with SURF and Tim Fröhlich to build a schema-agnostic hybrid search system for orchestrator-core, funded by GÉANT. Shipped in v5.0."
  lang={lang}
>
  <aside class="header-overview" data-header-overview aria-label="Header overview">
    <span class="header-overview-title">Overview</span>
    <nav data-header-overview-list></nav>
  </aside>

  <article class="case-post">
    <div class="container">
      <a href={`/${lang}/cases/`} class="back-link">← All cases</a>

      <header class="case-header">
        <div class="case-eyebrow-row">
          <span class="cases-eyebrow">Case Study</span>
          <div class="case-tags">
            <span class="tag">AI Search</span>
            <span class="tag">RAG</span>
            <span class="tag">Open Source</span>
            <span class="tag">Network Orchestration</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <h1>Hybrid search for Orchestrator-Core</h1>
        <p class="case-subtitle">Schema-agnostic search for SURF's network infrastructure, shipped as open source in orchestrator-core v5.0</p>

        <div class="case-partner-logos">
          <a href="https://www.surf.nl" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="partner-logo-wrap">
            <img src="/images/cases/surf-orchestrator-core/surf-logo.png" alt="SURF" class="partner-logo" />
          </a>
          <a href="https://geant.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="partner-logo-wrap">
            <img src="/images/cases/surf-orchestrator-core/geant-logo.png" alt="GÉANT" class="partner-logo partner-logo--wide" />
          </a>
          <a href="https://github.com/workfloworchestrator" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="partner-logo-wrap partner-logo-wrap--dark">
            <img src="/images/cases/surf-orchestrator-core/wfo-logo.png" alt="Workflow Orchestrator" class="partner-logo partner-logo--square" />
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="case-meta-row">
          <div class="case-meta-item">
            <span class="case-meta-label">Client</span>
            <span>SURF</span>
          </div>
          <div class="case-meta-item">
            <span class="case-meta-label">Collaborator</span>
            <span>Tim Fröhlich</span>
          </div>
          <div class="case-meta-item">
            <span class="case-meta-label">Funded by</span>
            <span>GÉANT GN5-2 Incubator</span>
          </div>
          <div class="case-meta-item">
            <span class="case-meta-label">Stack</span>
            <span>Python · PostgreSQL · pgvector · pg_trgm · ltree · PydanticAI</span>
          </div>
          <div class="case-meta-item">
            <span class="case-meta-label">Released</span>
            <a href="https://workfloworchestrator.org/orchestrator-core/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">orchestrator-core v5.0 ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="case-meta-item">
            <span class="case-meta-label">GitHub</span>
            <a href="https://github.com/workfloworchestrator" target="_blank" rel="noopener">workfloworchestrator ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="post-content case-content">
        <h2>The challenge</h2>
        <p><a href="https://workfloworchestrator.org/orchestrator-core/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Orchestrator-core</a> is an open-source framework for managing product lifecycles and workflows for network infrastructure. It was built by and for the NREN community: National Research and Education Networks like SURF, which runs it to manage subscriptions, services, and configurations across more than 100 Dutch educational and research institutions, and GÉANT, the pan-European backbone that connects them all.</p>

        <p>The problem was search. Orchestrator-core's domain models are user-defined: operators assemble products from reusable product blocks, which can nest arbitrarily. A single subscription can contain hundreds of attributes spread across deeply nested structures. The schema isn't fixed. It evolves whenever someone defines a new product type.</p>

        <p>Traditional search doesn't work here. Elasticsearch needs a known schema. Static column indexes can't track a structure that doesn't exist until runtime. Simple <code>LIKE</code> queries don't understand meaning. For operators managing thousands of subscriptions, finding anything required clicking through nested pages by hand.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="post-content case-content">
        <h2>The collaboration</h2>
        <p>SURF initiated the project and secured funding through the GÉANT GN5-2 Incubator program. Tim Fröhlich designed and built the core search system. Virge contributed the AI agent layer: the type-safe query DSL, the PydanticAI integration, and the three-phase agent architecture that makes natural language search production-safe.</p>

        <p>Small team. Six months. Shipped in orchestrator-core v5.0 under Apache 2.0.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="post-content case-content">
        <h2>The solution</h2>
        <p>Everything runs on PostgreSQL. No Elasticsearch cluster, no separate vector database, no extra infrastructure to operate or scale.</p>

        <p>The foundation is Entity-Attribute-Value indexing with hierarchical paths. Instead of mapping dynamic schemas to fixed columns, each attribute gets its own index row: a path (stored with PostgreSQL's <code>ltree</code> extension), a typed value, and an optional embedding vector. A field like <code>product.interface.speed</code> becomes a traversable path. New product types are searchable the moment they're defined. No migrations, no reindexing.</p>

        <p>Three retrievers run in parallel on top of that index:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>pgvector</strong>: semantic search. Finds results by meaning, not just matching text.</li>
          <li><strong>pg_trgm</strong>: fuzzy text matching. Catches typos, partial matches, and exact ID searches that semantic search would miss.</li>
          <li><strong>Structured filters</strong>: typed predicates on dates, enums, booleans, and UUIDs.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Reciprocal Rank Fusion merges all three into a single ranking. Each retriever contributes its own ordering; RRF combines them without score normalization. The result: a search that handles "amsterdam network" and "sub-550e8400" equally well.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Architecture diagram -->
      <div class="search-arch-diagram article-illustration">
        <div class="diagram-bar">
          <span class="diagram-label">Search architecture</span>
          <span class="diagram-note">PostgreSQL-native · no external services</span>
        </div>
        <div class="arch-grid">
          <!-- EAV index: spans all 3 retriever rows -->
          <div class="arch-node arch-node-index arch-eav">
            <span class="arch-node-label">EAV index</span>
            <span class="arch-node-sub">ltree · typed values · embeddings</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Left fan-out: one arrow per retriever -->
          <div class="arch-arr arch-lr1" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="arch-arr arch-lr2" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="arch-arr arch-lr3" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <!-- Retrievers: one per row -->
          <div class="arch-node arch-node-retriever arch-r1">
            <span class="arch-node-icon">&#x1F9E0;</span>
            <span class="arch-node-label">pgvector</span>
            <span class="arch-node-sub">semantic similarity</span>
          </div>
          <div class="arch-node arch-node-retriever arch-r2">
            <span class="arch-node-icon">&#x1F50D;</span>
            <span class="arch-node-label">pg_trgm</span>
            <span class="arch-node-sub">fuzzy text</span>
          </div>
          <div class="arch-node arch-node-retriever arch-r3">
            <span class="arch-node-icon">&#x1F3F7;</span>
            <span class="arch-node-label">filters</span>
            <span class="arch-node-sub">typed predicates</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Right fan-in: one arrow per retriever -->
          <div class="arch-arr arch-rr1" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="arch-arr arch-rr2" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="arch-arr arch-rr3" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <!-- RRF: spans all 3 rows -->
          <div class="arch-node arch-node-rrf arch-rrf">
            <span class="arch-node-label">RRF</span>
            <span class="arch-node-sub">Reciprocal Rank Fusion</span>
          </div>
          <!-- Final arrow + output: span all 3 rows -->
          <div class="arch-arr arch-arr--final arch-final-arr" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="arch-node arch-node-output arch-output">
            <span class="arch-node-label">Ranked results</span>
            <span class="arch-node-sub">cursor-paginated</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="post-content case-content">
        <h2>Safe for AI agents</h2>
        <p>Raw SQL generation by an LLM is a bad idea. One hallucinated <code>DROP TABLE</code> and the day is ruined. We built a Pydantic-based query DSL that compiles to validated SQL. The agent never touches query strings directly.</p>

        <p>The same Pydantic models that define the DSL serve as typed tool parameters for PydanticAI. The agent fills in a structured form; the system compiles and validates it before anything reaches the database. The agent can construct filters, sorting, aggregations, and pagination, all without generating a single line of SQL.</p>

        <p>The agent workflow runs in three phases:</p>
      </div>

      <MermaidFlow diagram={agentWorkflow} />

      <div class="post-content case-content">
        <p>This means an operator can ask "show me all 10Gbps interfaces in Amsterdam provisioned last month" and get back accurate, paginated results. No raw query involved.</p>

        <h2>The outcome</h2>
        <p>Hybrid search shipped in orchestrator-core v5.0, Apache 2.0. Any organization running orchestrator-core gets it out of the box. No configuration, no extra infrastructure. SURF's operators can now search across thousands of subscriptions and workflows in seconds.</p>

        <p>Incremental indexing uses SHA-256 content hashing to skip re-embedding unchanged fields, so the index stays current without full rebuilds. Keyset pagination embeds a <code>(score, entity_id, query_id)</code> cursor so result sets stay stable even when the underlying data changes mid-session. The EAV approach scales to millions of indexed attributes across deeply nested schemas.</p>

        <p>For the full technical write-up (EAV implementation, retriever routing, keyset pagination, and agent architecture), see Tim Fröhlich's post: <a href="https://timfrohlich.com/blog/postgresql-hybrid-search" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Building a Schema-Agnostic Hybrid Search System in PostgreSQL ↗</a></p>

        <h2>Since then</h2>
        <p>At the <a href="https://workfloworchestrator.org/meetings/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">third Workflow Orchestrator user meeting</a> (TNC26 Helsinki, June 2026), the community reported on the first year of this system in the wild. It has a name now: AI Search. Version 5.0 made it the default and deprecated the old Postgres full-text search. Every organization upgrading to 5.0 runs it, whether they use the AI features or not; connecting an LLM for semantic search stays optional and off by default.</p>

        <p>The retriever set grew to five: structured filters, fuzzy trigram matching, semantic embeddings, and two hybrid combinations, all on the same EAV index described above.</p>

        <p>The search engine also became the foundation for <code>orchestrator-agent</code>, a natural-language agent that answers plain-language questions about subscriptions, products, workflows, and processes. It reuses this search engine directly and exposes it over MCP, A2A, and AG-UI. The WFO community now counts "AI &amp; agents" among the five core themes of its ecosystem.</p>
      </div>

      <CTA lang={lang} />
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<script>
  // Heading overview (desktop panel + mobile sheet) and its collision guard are
  // handled centrally in Layout.astro.
  function initCaseCodeCopy() {
    const labels = { copy: 'Copy', copied: 'Copied', fallback: 'Code' };
    const languageLabels = {
      bash: 'Bash', css: 'CSS', dotenv: 'ENV', html: 'HTML',
      js: 'JavaScript', json: 'JSON', md: 'Markdown', markdown: 'Markdown',
      py: 'Python', python: 'Python', sh: 'Shell', ts: 'TypeScript',
      yaml: 'YAML', yml: 'YAML',
    };

    function getCodeBlockTitle(pre) {
      const code = pre.querySelector('code');
      const languageClass = Array.from(code?.classList || [])
        .find((c) => c.startsWith('language-'));
      const language = languageClass?.replace('language-', '') || pre.dataset.language || '';
      return languageLabels[language.toLowerCase()] || language.toUpperCase() || labels.fallback;
    }

    document.querySelectorAll('.case-post pre').forEach((pre) => {
      if (pre.parentElement?.classList.contains('code-block-shell')) return;
      const wrapper = document.createElement('div');
      wrapper.className = 'code-block-shell article-illustration';
      pre.parentNode?.insertBefore(wrapper, pre);
      const toolbar = document.createElement('div');
      toolbar.className = 'code-block-toolbar';
      const title = document.createElement('span');
      title.className = 'code-block-title';
      title.textContent = getCodeBlockTitle(pre);
      const button = document.createElement('button');
      button.type = 'button';
      button.className = 'code-copy-btn';
      button.textContent = labels.copy;
      toolbar.append(title, button);
      wrapper.appendChild(toolbar);
      wrapper.appendChild(pre);
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const code = pre.querySelector('code')?.textContent || pre.textContent || '';
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code);
          button.textContent = labels.copied;
          button.classList.add('is-copied');
          window.setTimeout(() => {
            button.textContent = labels.copy;
            button.classList.remove('is-copied');
          }, 1500);
        } catch {
          button.textContent = labels.copy;
        }
      });
    });
  }

  function initCaseIllustrations() {
    document
      .querySelectorAll('.case-screenshot, .screenshot-placeholder, .search-arch-diagram, .case-content img, .case-content svg, .case-content figure')
      .forEach((el) => el.classList.add('article-illustration'));
  }

  initCaseCodeCopy();
  initCaseIllustrations();
</script>

<style>
  .case-post {
    --case-content-width: 720px;
    --case-visual-width: 860px;
    --case-flow-width: 860px;
    padding: 2rem 0 4rem;
  }

  .case-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(108,92,231,0.16);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 84% 20%, rgba(168,85,247,0.18), transparent 28%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.035), rgba(255,255,255,0.01));
  }

  .case-eyebrow-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .case-subtitle {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 1.18rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  /* Partner logos */
  .case-partner-logos {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .partner-logo-wrap {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    height: 52px;
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0 0.9rem;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;
  }

  .partner-logo-wrap:hover {
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .partner-logo {
    height: 32px;
    width: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
    display: block;
  }

  .partner-logo--square {
    height: 52px;
    width: 52px;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .partner-logo-wrap--dark {
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .case-meta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 2rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .case-meta-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .case-meta-label {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent2);
  }

  .case-meta-item span:not(.case-meta-label),
  .case-meta-item a {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .case-content {
    max-width: var(--case-content-width);
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .case-content h2 {
    scroll-margin-top: 6rem;
  }

  .case-content code {
    font-size: 0.85em;
    background: rgba(108,92,231,0.12);
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--accent2);
  }

  .case-content ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .case-content ul li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  /* Architecture diagram */
  .search-arch-diagram {
    width: min(100%, var(--case-visual-width));
    margin: 1.5rem auto 2.5rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(108,92,231,0.14);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: rgba(18,18,42,0.36);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Caption bar matches FlowDiagram component */
  .diagram-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 1rem;
    background: rgba(108,92,231,0.1);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(108,92,231,0.14);
  }

  .diagram-label {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent2);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .diagram-note {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1;
  }

  /* Grid: EAV → [fan-out arrows] → retrievers → [fan-in arrows] → RRF → arrow → output */
  .arch-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1.75rem 1fr 1.75rem auto 1.75rem auto;
    grid-template-rows: repeat(3, 1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem 0;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    scrollbar-width: none;
  }
  .arch-grid::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }

  /* Grid placement */
  .arch-eav        { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1 / span 3; }
  .arch-lr1        { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1; }
  .arch-lr2        { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 2; }
  .arch-lr3        { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 3; }
  .arch-r1         { grid-column: 3; grid-row: 1; }
  .arch-r2         { grid-column: 3; grid-row: 2; }
  .arch-r3         { grid-column: 3; grid-row: 3; }
  .arch-rr1        { grid-column: 4; grid-row: 1; }
  .arch-rr2        { grid-column: 4; grid-row: 2; }
  .arch-rr3        { grid-column: 4; grid-row: 3; }
  .arch-rrf        { grid-column: 5; grid-row: 1 / span 3; }
  .arch-final-arr  { grid-column: 6; grid-row: 1 / span 3; align-self: center; }
  .arch-output     { grid-column: 7; grid-row: 1 / span 3; }

  /* Arrow cells horizontal lines with arrowhead */
  .arch-arr {
    height: 1px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(108,92,231,0.45), rgba(168,85,247,0.75));
    position: relative;
    align-self: center;
  }
  .arch-arr::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    right: -1px;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    width: 0; height: 0;
    border-top: 3px solid transparent;
    border-bottom: 3px solid transparent;
    border-left: 5px solid rgba(168,85,247,0.75);
  }
  .arch-arr--final {
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2));
  }
  .arch-arr--final::before {
    border-left-color: var(--accent2);
    border-top-width: 4px;
    border-bottom-width: 4px;
    border-left-width: 6px;
  }

  /* Nodes */
  .arch-node {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(108,92,231,0.22);
    background: rgba(108,92,231,0.08);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .arch-node-index {
    border-color: rgba(168,85,247,0.3);
    background: rgba(168,85,247,0.07);
  }

  .arch-node-rrf {
    border-color: rgba(168,85,247,0.4);
    background: rgba(168,85,247,0.12);
  }

  .arch-node-output {
    border-color: rgba(108,231,130,0.3);
    background: rgba(108,231,130,0.06);
  }

  .arch-node-icon { font-size: 1.1rem; }

  .arch-node-label {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .arch-node-sub {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .case-meta-row { gap: 1rem; }

    /* Stack arch grid vertically: EAV → retrievers (3) → RRF → output */
    .arch-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      grid-template-rows: none;
      gap: 0.5rem;
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .arch-eav        { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; }
    .arch-lr1, .arch-lr2, .arch-lr3,
    .arch-rr1, .arch-rr2, .arch-rr3  { display: none; }
    .arch-r1         { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; }
    .arch-r2         { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; }
    .arch-r3         { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; }
    .arch-rrf        { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; }
    .arch-final-arr  { display: none; }
    .arch-output     { grid-column: 1; grid-row: auto; }

    .arch-node { width: 100%; }
  }
</style>
